The city feels like one of those comparative realms where quiet streets and bright towers live together.  
Its lamps emit a soft glow, and likewise the river seems to emit patience as it moves.  
I felt a profound change when I learned to adjust my pace and notice small, certain details.  
A durable friendship can pull two people through hard seasons, and likewise through joyful ones.  
