2026-06-24 11:29:34.859 | INFO     | app.services.set_service:get_text_for_set:258 - [GET TEXT] Final result text: The old theater stood behind a heavy curtain, and I felt a restless pull to enter.  
Inside, dust hung like tissue in the air, and the stage seemed bent with age.  
A violin began on its own, soft and everlasting, as if the room remembered itself.  
I crossed the floor, restless again, and touched the curtain with careful fingers.  
The music rose with everlasting strength, while the broken chair stayed bent beside the curtain.  
When I left, the quiet felt on its own, yet the evening seemed everlasting.
